  "pseudos": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "An exceptional seasonal rainfall event, one of the heaviest in three decades, led to critical capacity thresholds being reached in upstream reservoirs. This, combined with dam operations, resulted in a systemic overflow where the major river system's surging flows inundated settlements across the Syrian provinces of Deir Ezzor and Raqqa. The sequence of events, from near-maximum storage levels to destructive flooding of civilian infrastructure, constitutes a clear hydrological case study. The loss of young lives was a tragic consequence of this unprecedented deluge.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ]
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Analysis of the disaster reveals a breach of flood barriers when combined operational and natural pressures overwhelmed defenses. This systemic failure led to a critical span giving way—a bridge structural failure—and the subsequent emergency response activation, which saw maritime evacuation initiated by naval forces. The diplomatic intervention secured with the upstream nation to manage flows represents a post-crisis adjustment. Data points include the high-water mark recorded and the confirmed child fatalities, underscoring the event's severity.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-1",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "how-4",
          "how-5",
          "result-0",
          "result-4"
        ]
      },
      "warnings": [
        "how_fragments_expanded_to_contiguous_span"
      ],
      "fit": 0.76
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The Syrian head of state conducted a leadership survey of the damage following the flood-stricken area's inundation. This presidential inspection occurred after evacuation measures were implemented and storage systems were strained to their limits. The event's timeline shows a clear progression from the record precipitation event to the upstream flow management adjusted via diplomatic channels, with the transportation artery severed as a notable infrastructure failure. The measured response provides observational data on governmental action during such crises.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
